// 소스를 연 채로 인용을 적는다. 요약이 아니라 원문과 그 위치다. locator 는 원문의 절 제목(§)이고, 그림 값은 "Figure N (image)" 다.
{"id":"e1","source":"w1","locator":"§intro","quote":"many applications using Claude Platform can cut costs without giving up performance with three fixes: maximize the prompt cache hit rate, remove anti-patterns from your prompts when upgrading to frontier Claude models, and calibrate effort to the task. We've put this guidance into the claude-api skill","why":"글 전체의 주장과 세 축, 그리고 skill 로 옮겼다는 선언"}
{"id":"e2","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache","quote":"This step, called prefill, is the expensive part of handling input. Prompt caching saves that state (the key–value, or KV, cache): when a request starts with the same prefix, Claude reads it back instead of recomputing it. Cache reads are billed at a fraction of the full input price.","why":"캐시가 무엇을 저장하는지"}
{"id":"e3","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache","quote":"First, the prompt cache is pinned to a specific model. Second, prompt cache reads must be byte-exact across the full span of the prompt. Finally, the prompt cache has a limited time-to-live (TTL).","why":"캐시의 세 제약"}
{"id":"e4","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · tips","quote":"Avoid changing effort or thinking settings mid-conversation. These settings render into the prompt ahead of your content, so they are part of the cached prefix. With Claude Opus 5 and Fable 5.1 specifically, you can update effort mid-conversation without breaking the cache.","why":"effort 가 prefix 에 들어간다는 것과 예외 모델 두 개"}
{"id":"e5","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · tips","quote":"Keep volatile values out of the prefix. A dynamic timestamp or ID in the system prompt can change across model calls, and break the cache.","why":"캐시를 깨는 원인 2"}
{"id":"e6","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · tips","quote":"When using the Claude Messages API, the prompt is assembled in a fixed order with tool definitions rendered at the top. Any change to the tool definition will break the cache.","why":"도구 정의가 맨 위라 바뀌면 전부 깨진다"}
{"id":"e7","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · tips","quote":"Subagents and branches only share the parent's cache when the fork's prefix is byte-identical, on the same model, and using the same effort.","why":"fork 조건 세 가지"}
{"id":"e8","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · tips","quote":"If an agent blocks on a long-running tool call or sub-agent, the cache can expire before the results come back. The next turn has to rewrite the cache, at 1.25× the normal input price (2× for a 1-hour cache) instead of the cheap read price.","why":"TTL 초과의 비용: 쓰기 1.25x, 1시간 캐시 2x"}
{"id":"e9","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"Claude Console provides prompt cache diagnostics, including reasoning for prompt cache misses (Figure 1). If hits drop unexpectedly, the cache diagnostics API tells you exactly where two requests diverged.","why":"진단 도구 두 가지"}
{"id":"e10","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"Declare all your tools up front but mark the rarely used ones defer_loading: they stay out of the cached prefix and are appended into the conversation only when Claude looks them up with tool search, so the cache is preserved.","why":"defer_loading 동작"}
{"id":"e11","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"Claude Platform lets you add a system instruction as a message mid-conversation instead of editing the system prompt, which preserves the cache.","why":"system prompt 대신 message 로"}
{"id":"e12","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"Certain operations, like compaction, already rewrite much of the cache (the conversation). That is a good moment to switch model or effort, since you are paying for a miss anyway.","why":"모델·effort 변경 타이밍"}
{"id":"e13","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"With Claude Platform, you can set automatic caching to automatically apply the cache breakpoint to the last cacheable block.","why":"breakpoint 이동을 자동화"}
{"id":"e14","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"To reduce latency, send a request with max_tokens: 0 and an explicit cache breakpoint. This processes the prompt and writes it to the cache without generating anything.","why":"pre-warm 방법"}
{"id":"e15","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt cache · How to fix it","quote":"The 5-minute cache TTL counts from the start of the request. If an agent blocks on tool calls or sub-agent requests that run longer than 5 minutes, the parent's cache expires before the result comes back. In cases like this, consider setting a 1-hour TTL on the prefix instead.","why":"TTL 기산점과 1시간 TTL 권고"}
{"id":"e16","source":"w1","locator":"Figure 1 (image)","quote":"Cache read ratio 71.3% (↑8.2% vs previous 7 days) · Cache read tokens 12.4B (↑11.4%) · Claude Opus 5: Cache misses 28.4k, Total missed tokens 1.2B · Missed tokens by reason: Messages changed / System changed / Tools changed / Model changed","why":"Console 진단 화면에 있는 값. 본문 텍스트에는 없다"}
{"id":"e17","source":"w1","locator":"Figure 2 (image)","quote":"System instructions (globally cached) · Tools (globally cached) · CLAUDE.md, memory (cached per project) · Session state (cached per session) · Messages (grows each turn)","why":"안정 prefix 다섯 층의 순서와 캐시 범위"}
{"id":"e18","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions","quote":"Verification rituals. Instructions like \"double-check your work\" or \"verify twice before responding\" are often taken literally by frontier models and can waste tokens.","why":"anti-pattern 1"}
{"id":"e19","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions","quote":"Contradictory rules. Frontier models are better at instruction following. Contradictory instructions (\"always refund within policy\" vs. \"never issue refunds without escalation\") can be followed more literally by frontier models, resulting in degraded performance.","why":"anti-pattern 5. 정확도를 깎는 종류"}
{"id":"e20","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions","quote":"Dated configuration. Settings written for an older Claude generation (e.g., manual thinking budgets) can be rejected by the Claude Platform when upgrading to frontier models.","why":"anti-pattern 6. API 가 거부하는 종류"}
{"id":"e21","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions · How to fix it","quote":"In Claude Code, run /claude-api prompt-audit against your prompts, skills, or tool descriptions. The audit covers anything in your working directory, including application code that calls the Claude API and Claude Code's own configuration (e.g., CLAUDE.md or skills).","why":"prompt-audit 의 범위"}
{"id":"e22","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions · How to fix it","quote":"We started from a clean prompt and planted one anti-pattern at a time (a retired thinking setting, a pair of contradictory refund rules, a manual scratchpad, \"verify twice\", \"be maximally thorough\", and a mandatory six-step procedure), giving six legacy prompts.","why":"실험 설계: 심은 anti-pattern 여섯 개"}
{"id":"e23","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions · How to fix it","quote":"Running /claude-api prompt-audit removed the anti-patterns, decreasing costs by 14.6% and increasing accuracy by 5.3% on average.","why":"prompt-audit 효과의 대표 수치"}
{"id":"e24","source":"w1","locator":"§Instructions · How to fix it","quote":"The retired thinking setting made the API reject every routing request outright. The contradictory refund rules led Opus 5 to withhold four refunds it owed while it asked the customer to confirm. And the manual scratchpad collided with Opus 5's built-in thinking: on three tickets it wrote the tool call inside its reasoning and never executed it.","why":"정확도가 오른 세 가지 이유"}
{"id":"e25","source":"w1","locator":"Figure 3 (image)","quote":"Opus 4.8 legacy 2.52¢ · 89.4% → (model upgrade) Opus 5 unaudited 3.43¢ · 91.7% → (audit step: +5.3 pts, −0.49¢) Opus 5 audited 2.93¢ · 97.0%","why":"세 점의 절대값. 본문에는 평균 변화율만 있다"}
{"id":"e26","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort","quote":"Claude Fable 5 scores 11.5% at low effort for $5.35 per task on FrontierCode Diamond (the hardest 50 tasks). At max effort, Fable 5 gets 30.9% for $19.00 per task; changing effort raises the score about 2.7x (+19 points) for about 3.5x the cost (Figure 4).","why":"effort 가 값을 하는 경우의 수치"}
{"id":"e27","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort","quote":"It scores about 53% at low effort for about $0.30 per question and about 61% at max effort for about $2.23; the last step up to max adds about half a point for 46% more cost. The gain inside the benchmark's run-to-run noise, so you pay more for no measurable gain.","why":"HLE 에서 마지막 단계가 값을 못 하는 수치. 마지막 문장은 원문 그대로 동사가 빠져 있다"}
{"id":"e28","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort","quote":"Set too low, Claude stops before it has enough evidence. It makes fewer tool calls, so it may answer from the first search result instead of the third. It thinks less on hard steps and skips the check it would normally run on its own. The answer looks finished, but it's built on partial information.","why":"낮은 effort 의 실패 모양"}
{"id":"e29","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"on CursorBench 3.2, Claude Fable 5.1 at low effort matches the performance of Fable 5 at high effort at a third of the cost (Figure 5). Two things make the newer model cheaper: at low effort it does less work per task, and Fable 5.1's prompt-cache reads are priced at $0.25 per million tokens versus $1.00 for Fable 5. Even at Fable 5's prices, Fable 5.1 at low effort would cost about 40% less.","why":"강한 모델 낮은 effort 의 근거와 가격 요인 분리"}
{"id":"e30","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"On a non-saturated evaluation, a flat performance-cost curve across effort levels suggests that the task is not bound by thinking compute; increasing effort is not beneficial.","why":"곡선 모양으로 판단하는 규칙"}
{"id":"e31","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"In Claude Code, /claude-api hillclimb performs this search for you: it splits your evaluation into train and test sets, proposes configuration changes, and reads failing train examples to fix what it finds.","why":"hillclimb 정의"}
{"id":"e32","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"The hillclimber first tried Opus 5 at low effort, applying prompt-audit to remove mandatory tool-call rituals, scratchpad steps, and contradictory rules. That cleared the Opus 4.8 baseline at 98.9% train accuracy and cut cost to 2.6 cents per ticket.","why":"hillclimb 1단계"}
{"id":"e33","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"It then stepped down to Sonnet 5 at low effort, which was cheaper still at 1 cent per ticket, but accuracy fell to 88.9%. Reading the failing train tickets, Claude added routing rules and a refund-cap cross-reference to the prompt, bringing Sonnet 5 back to 98.9% at the same cost.","why":"hillclimb 2·3단계"}
{"id":"e34","source":"w1","locator":"§Effort · How to fix it","quote":"On the 14 held-out tickets the search never saw, the final configuration scored 90.5% against the original setup's 78.6%, at about one fifth the cost.","why":"held-out 결과. n=14"}
{"id":"e35","source":"w1","locator":"Figure 6 (image)","quote":"1 · Opus 4.8 | high effort (baseline) · starting accuracy, 74.4% → 2 · Opus 5 | low effort (move to higher tier & audit prompt) → 3 · Sonnet 5 | low effort (drop to Sonnet 5 at low effort) → 4 · Sonnet 5 | low effort (improve prompt). y: decision accuracy (%, train split). legend: adopted path · train-split read","why":"train split 의 출발점 74.4% 는 그림에만 있다"}
{"id":"e36","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"cost-optimize starts by finding where your tokens go: from your organization's usage and cost reports if you have a Claude Admin API key, from the usage object on each API response if your application logs it, or, failing both, by reading your request-building code and estimating.","why":"cost-optimize 의 프로파일 소스 세 단계"}
{"id":"e37","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"It then ranks the available savings, starting with prompt caching, trimming what each request carries (including a prompt-audit), bounding output, and batching unattended work. If you supply an evaluation, it goes further and computes cost and performance across effort levels and model choices.","why":"레버 순서와 eval 유무의 차이"}
{"id":"e38","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"LegalBench (~58% lower cost):  cost-optimize proposed caching a shared prefix across tasks, setting low effort, and processing tasks via the Batch API. Thinking tokens fell from 102,779 to 8,284, but pass rate stayed within noise and cost dropped by ~58%.","why":"사례 1"}
{"id":"e39","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"tau2-bench retail (~73% lower cost): By implementing prompt caching with explicit breakpoint placement, cost-optimize reduced spend by 73% while keeping pass rate flat.","why":"사례 2"}
{"id":"e40","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"OfficeQA Pro (~52% lower cost): cost-optimize added batch processing and document caching, which brought cost down from $136.20 to $64.87.","why":"사례 3"}
{"id":"e41","source":"w1","locator":"§Automating cost reduction","quote":"SWE-bench Verified (~55% lower cost): cost-optimize found that the default config already caches correctly. Savings came from setting effort to medium and constraining the agent's output to just a few concise sentences. Median steps per task went from 29 to 17 and prompt tokens fell from 75.2M to 33.7M.","why":"사례 4"}
{"id":"e42","source":"w1","locator":"Figure 7 (image)","quote":"tau2-bench (retail) −72.7% $25.88 → $7.05, +1.3pp (95% CI −4.6 to +7.2) · LegalBench −57.6% $13.67 → $5.79, −0.3pp (95% CI −0.8 to +0.3) · OfficeQA Pro −52.4% $136.20 → $64.87, +4.5pp (95% CI −2.1 to +11.1) · SWE-bench Verified −55.1% $39.74 → $17.86, −3.3pp (95% CI −9.6 to +3.1). 'starting with Sonnet 5 as a baseline'","why":"네 사례의 정확한 비용과 점수 변화·신뢰구간. 본문은 대략값만 적는다"}
{"id":"e43","source":"w1","locator":"§Getting started","quote":"Start with /claude-api prompt-audit when you've migrated to a frontier Claude model and want to check your existing prompts against it. ... Reach for /claude-api cost-optimize when your application uses the Claude API and you want a cost audit. ... Finally, use /claude-api hillclimb for an iterative search over cost and performance. Given an evaluation, Claude splits it into train and test sets, then proposes updates to your application that aim to reduce cost while maintaining baseline performance.","why":"세 명령을 언제 쓰는지의 원문 안내"}
{"id":"e44","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/SKILL.md:57-62 (Subcommands 표)","quote":"| `migrate` | ... | `prompt-audit` | Audit existing prompts, skills, and tool descriptions for dated patterns (\"cruft\") written for older models. **Read `shared/prompt-audit.md` immediately** ... | `upgrade` | ... | `cost-optimize` | Reduce what existing Claude API code costs to run, without sacrificing output quality. **Read `shared/cost-optimization.md` immediately**","why":"고정 커밋의 subcommand 는 migrate / prompt-audit / upgrade / cost-optimize 네 개. hillclimb 없음"}
{"id":"e45","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:12","quote":"once the project has an eval, the levers become a hillclimb - one change at a time against the eval, keep or revert (Step 3).","why":"저장소에서 hillclimb 라는 단어가 나오는 유일한 자리. 명령이 아니라 Step 3 의 설명"}
{"id":"e46","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/prompt-audit.md:9-10","quote":"1. **An audit report**: every finding with its location (`file:line`), the pattern it matches, why it is obsolete for the target model, and a confidence level. 2. **A proposed diff**: concrete edits for the findings that warrant them. Propose - never apply edits without the user's consent.","why":"prompt-audit 의 산출물 두 개"}
{"id":"e47","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/prompt-audit.md:18","quote":"This audit is non-interactive by design: it runs the same way in a chat session, a CI job, or a batch migration, so it states its assumptions and proceeds instead of pausing for confirmation.","why":"prompt-audit 는 묻지 않고 돈다"}
{"id":"e48","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/prompt-audit.md:43","quote":"For each instruction, ask one question: **could the model already know this?**","why":"삭제 규칙의 한 줄"}
{"id":"e49","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/prompt-audit.md:175-176","quote":"1. **Context is never cruft.** Audience, product, environment facts, quality bar, constraints, and the *reasons* for them - what only the author knows. ... 2. **Cruft != length.** The harm comes from specific outdated instructions, not from volume. Never justify a deletion by character count alone.","why":"keep list. 지우지 않는 것"}
{"id":"e50","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:8-10","quote":"**Free wins** - prompt caching, input-token hygiene (including a prompt audit), loop hygiene, output-token hygiene, batch processing - lower what you pay without lowering output quality. They go first, and caching stays on permanently. **Tradeoffs** - budgets, effort, model choice, multi-model architectures - exchange cost for intelligence. They go last","why":"cost-optimize 의 레버 두 종류와 순서"}
{"id":"e51","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:20","quote":"Unlike the prompt audit, this workflow is interactive by design: when context for a lever is missing, or a step would spend real money, work through it with the user rather than assuming.","why":"cost-optimize 는 대화형. prompt-audit 와 반대"}
{"id":"e52","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:181","quote":"**Ask for the measurement budget once, not per run.** Present the validation plan with its total expected runs and cost","why":"돈 쓰는 실행은 승인이 필요하다"}
{"id":"e53","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/SKILL.md:242 (Thinking & Effort)","quote":"**Effort (GA, no beta header):** `output_config: {effort: \"low\"|\"medium\"|\"high\"|\"xhigh\"|\"max\"}` - inside `output_config`, not top-level; default `high` (equivalent to omitting it).","why":"effort 파라미터 위치와 다섯 단계, 기본값 high"}
{"id":"e54","source":"d1","locator":"§Change effort mid-conversation / Per-message effort (beta)","quote":"Per-message effort is in beta and requires the beta header `mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01`. Models without per-message effort, including Claude Fable 5, return a 400 error ... Add a `role: \"system\"` message with empty `content` and the new level in `output_config.effort`.","why":"원문이 말한 Opus 5 / Fable 5.1 의 mid-conversation effort 변경의 실제 방법"}
{"id":"e55","source":"d2","locator":"§Prompt caching pricing 표 + 각주 1","quote":"5-minute cache write | 1.25x base input price ... 1-hour cache write | 2x base input price ... Cache read (hit) | 0.1x base input price (0.025x on Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1)","why":"원문의 1.25x/2x 와 $0.25 vs $1.00 의 출처"}
{"id":"e56","source":"d4","locator":"§Compatibility, 본문 19행","quote":"Beta header: `cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07` ... On your next request, include that `id` as `diagnostics.previous_message_id`. The API rebuilds the fingerprint for the new request, compares it against the stored one, and attaches a `diagnostics` object to the response describing the first point of divergence.","why":"원문이 '어디서 갈라졌는지 알려준다'고 한 API 의 실제 인터페이스"}
{"id":"e57","source":"d5","locator":"§What invalidates your cache","quote":"The cache follows a prefix hierarchy (`tools` → `system` → `messages`), so a change at one level invalidates that level and everything after it","why":"도구 정의가 맨 위라는 원문 설명의 근거"}
{"id":"e58","source":"d7","locator":"§Audit prompts against the current model","quote":"prompts written for Claude Opus 4.8 cost 36% more per ticket on Claude Opus 5 for no change in accuracy. Running the audit over the same prompts made Opus 5 both cheaper than the unaudited version (by 14%) and more accurate (97% of tickets, up from 92%, a gain outside the noise).","why":"같은 실험을 문서 페이지는 다른 반올림(14%, 97%/92%)으로 적는다. 블로그의 14.6%, 97.0%/91.7% 과 대조"}
{"id":"e59","source":"d3","locator":"§Automatic caching","quote":"Instead of placing `cache_control` on individual content blocks, add a single `cache_control` field at the top level of your request body. The system automatically applies the cache breakpoint to the last cacheable block.","why":"원문 'automatic caching' 의 실제 설정 방법"}
{"id":"e60","source":"d1","locator":"§Effort levels 표와 그 아래 문장","quote":"Not every model that supports `max` supports `xhigh`.","why":"09장 note 의 'max 는 되지만 xhigh 는 안 되는 모델이 있다'. 표에서 max 행은 Claude Mythos Preview, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.6 을 포함하고 xhigh 행은 셋을 뺀다. 2026-09-09 열람, 아카이브하지 않음"}
{"id":"e61","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/SKILL.md:55","quote":"If no table in the document matches, treat the request as normal prose.","why":"14장 note. hillclimb 처럼 Subcommands 표에 없는 문자열을 쳤을 때의 규칙"}
{"id":"e62","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:183","quote":"The published bar - around fifty cases and at least five trials per configuration - is the standard for the production cutover","why":"17장 2번. skill 자신의 측정 기준과 원문 held-out 14건의 대조"}
{"id":"e63","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:185","quote":"**Minimal eval recipe** - the cheapest thing that clears a tradeoff lever, so \"needs an eval\" is a next step rather than a dead end. Offer to build it with the user: - **Inputs**: a fixed set of ~20-30 real requests pulled from production logs or written by the user","why":"12장 note. 평가가 없을 때의 중간 경로"}
{"id":"e64","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/cost-optimization.md:181","quote":"Each lever that earns a place becomes **its own diff** (one lever per diff, so a revert is clean and effects attribute)","why":"14장 cost-optimize 행의 '레버당 diff 하나(되돌리기가 깨끗하도록)'"}
{"id":"e65","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/shared/prompt-audit.md:21","quote":"Resolve the target in this order: the model the request names; else the destination of an in-progress migration the repository documents (vendor notes, migration docs, TODOs); else the newest model the repository's own code or docs point at; else the current flagship","why":"14장 prompt-audit 행의 target 모델 결정 순서"}
{"id":"e66","source":"r1","locator":"skills/claude-api/LICENSE.txt:2","quote":"Apache License Version 2.0, January 2004","why":"14장 note 의 라이선스. SKILL.md:7 frontmatter 'license: Complete terms in LICENSE.txt' 가 이 파일을 가리킨다"}
{"id":"e67","source":"r1","locator":".claude-plugin/marketplace.json:46","quote":"\"name\": \"claude-api\", \"description\": \"Claude API and SDK documentation skill for building LLM-powered applications\", \"source\": \"./\", \"strict\": false, \"skills\": [ \"./skills/claude-api\" ]","why":"14장 note 의 설치 경로. marketplace 이름은 같은 파일 2행 'anthropic-agent-skills', 등록 명령은 README.md:36 '/plugin marketplace add anthropics/skills'"}
{"id":"e68","source":"d4","locator":"§Compatibility","quote":"Platforms: Claude API (beta); not available on Claude Platform on AWS, Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud, Microsoft Foundry","why":"06장 note 와 17장 c 의 cache diagnostics API 플랫폼 제한. 2026-09-09 열람, 아카이브하지 않음"}
{"id": "e69", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Change effort mid-conversation", "quote": "On Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, and Claude Opus 5, use a per-message effort change, which keeps the prompt cache. On other models, set a new top-level value on the next request, which starts the cache over.", "why": "04장 1행과 15장. 원문의 두 모델 언급을 배타적 목록으로 읽지 않기 위한 platform 문서의 범위. 2026-09-09 열람"}
{"id": "e70", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Top-level effort on the next request", "quote": "Because top-level effort shapes the rendered prompt, changing it between requests doesn't preserve cached prefixes from earlier turns.", "why": "15장. 최상위 effort 변경은 모델과 무관하게 캐시를 깬다"}
{"id": "e71", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Instructions", "quote": "Thoroughness and emphasis boosters. \"Be maximally thorough,\" \"CRITICAL: YOU MUST ALWAYS…\" can lead to verbosity and extra tool calls when working with frontier models.", "why": "anti-pattern 2"}
{"id": "e72", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Instructions", "quote": "Mandatory procedures and scratchpad scaffolds. Fixed step processes (e.g., \"think step by step in a scratchpad\") or reasoning templates are rituals that frontier models don't need. This scaffolding can stack on top of native reasoning and use unnecessary tokens.", "why": "anti-pattern 3"}
{"id": "e73", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Instructions", "quote": "Stale examples. Few-shot examples tuned to an older model's failure modes can teach a frontier model to imitate long reasoning chains on requests that don't need them.", "why": "anti-pattern 4. 08장 실험에는 심지 않았다"}
{"id": "e74", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Instructions · How to fix it", "quote": "With Opus 5, verification rituals (\"verify twice\") use unnecessary tokens by duplicating order lookup on every refund. Emphasis boosters (\"be maximally thorough\") became dozens of unneeded knowledge-base searches.", "why": "07장 표 4열의 verification·thoroughness 행"}
{"id": "e75", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Instructions · How to fix it", "quote": "Cost dropped because extra tool calls and duplicated reasoning were eliminated. Accuracy rose for three reasons.", "why": "08장 비용 −14.6% 의 원인 문장"}
{"id": "e76", "source": "w1", "locator": "Figure 7 (image)", "quote": "cost per run, as a share of baseline · score change (percentage points)", "why": "13장 표 머리글의 단위. 축 라벨은 그림에만 있다"}
